From 7f558fdd66fc91dee5c3ce1bc61265bd0c8d212a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:17:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: send 802.2 frames without encap offload

A frame with a length where the type goes, such as an STP BPDU, carries
its LLC header in the payload. The native path builds its 802.11 frame
without a SNAP header, and the encap offload cannot be told to do the
same, so send these frames through the native path.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -5107,6 +5107,13 @@ static void __ieee80211_subif_start_xmit
 		goto out;
 	}
 
+	/* A frame with a length in place of the type, such as a BPDU, has its
+	 * LLC header in the payload, which the offload cannot be told about:
+	 * the normal path sends it as it is.
+	 */
+	if (unlikely(ntohs(ehdr->h_proto) < ETH_P_802_3_MIN))
+		goto skip_offload;
+
 	/*
 	 * If STA is invalid, use the multicast offload path when applicable.
 	 * In AP mode, drop the frame if there are no associated stations;
